\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The cycle reads the backward difference}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Take #{d=1}. The coboundary of a function is
#{(df)(c(x))=f(x+1)-f(x)}, and
##{(d^\dagger\alpha)(x)=\alpha(c(x-1))-\alpha(c(x)).}
For an arbitrary vertex function #{f}, with
#{a(x)=f(x+1)-f(x)}, the commutator on a function #{g} is the
cochain #{a(x)\,g(x+1)} on the edge based at #{x}, and the
commutator on an edge cochain #{\alpha} is the function
##{([D,f]\alpha)(x)=\bigl(f(x-1)-f(x)\bigr)\alpha(c(x-1)).}
Composing these two steps, the square on a function #{g} is
multiplication by #{-a(x-1)^2}, the backward difference, and
the square on an edge cochain is multiplication by #{-a(x)^2},
the difference on that edge. When #{a} is constant the two
factors agree, and both equal #{-a^2}.}
